## std.arch.x86.avx2 — AVX2 intrinsics for x86_64.
##
## STATUS (zig 0.16): BLOCKED. The pass-through target
## `zig's std.arch.x86.avx2` was REMOVED in zig 0.16 (the whole
## `std.arch.x86` namespace is gone from the stdlib), so the
## `_mm256_*` intrinsics surface has no zig-side implementation to
## forward to. The SIMD story for zag v1 is the @Vector mapping in
## docs/manual/24-simd.md (vector types, literals, element-wise ops,
## @reduce-based reductions) — this file exists so module discovery
## and the scaffold parse-regression have a target, and so a future
## zig release restoring the intrinsics namespace can re-wire the
## pass-through alias without touching the docs.
